/// Deliberately named like the standard library's module: this directory also holds a program
///  whose own `import graph` must take this file (property 1), while std::opt's
/// internal `import graph` in stdlib/rules.cml must still take the standard library's module
///  (property 2). It exports only `answer`, so a standard-library graph used in its place
/// fails at `graph::answer`, and this file used in place of the standard library fails at
/// `Program` inside rules.cml.
module graph

export func answer(): int {
    return 41
}